column27:
When a bookmark is deleted, the {{BookmarkIndexer}} calls {{object.id}} on a nil object:

{noformat}
  def parent_id(object)
    if object.nil?
      deleted_bookmark_info(object.id)
{noformat}

This triggers an exception, causing the reindexing batch to fail.

The {{BookmarkIndexer}} knows the ID associated with the deleted object, and should pass it to {{parent_id}}.

The work search help pop-up says this about entering non-canonical tags in one of the tag fields:

{quote}
If your phrase doesn't match a common tag exactly, it will find all tags containing the words in your phrase. Entering <kbd>People Doing Things</kbd>, for example, will also find works tagged <samp>Nice People Doing Things</samp>, <samp>People Doing Shady Things</samp>, and <samp>People Doing Things with Spoons</samp>.
{quote}

This works properly on production. However, when [I enter "People Doing Things" into the "Additional Tags" field in the work search|https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/search?utf8=%E2%9C%93&work_search%5Bquery%5D=&work_search%5Btitle%5D=&work_search%5Bcreators%5D=&work_search%5Brevised_at%5D=&work_search%5Bcomplete%5D=&work_search%5Bcrossover%5D=&work_search%5Bsingle_chapter%5D=0&work_search%5Bword_count%5D=&work_search%5Blanguage_id%5D=&work_search%5Bfandom_names%5D=&work_search%5Brating_ids%5D=&work_search%5Bcharacter_names%5D=&work_search%5Brelationship_names%5D=&work_search%5Bfreeform_names%5D=People+Doing+Things&work_search%5Bhits%5D=&work_search%5Bkudos_count%5D=&work_search%5Bcomments_count%5D=&work_search%5Bbookmarks_count%5D=&work_search%5Bsort_column%5D=&work_search%5Bsort_direction%5D=desc&commit=Search] on staging, I get 0 results, even though the tag ["bad people doing bad things"|https://test.archiveofourown.org/tags/bad%20people%20doing%20bad%20things] does exist on staging and has a couple of works in it that should probably appear in the search results.

This is related to the cucumber test [features/search/work_tags.feature:252|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/master/features/search/works_tags.feature#L252]:

{quote}
Scenario: Searching by additional tags (freeforms) for a synonym of a meta tag returns works using (a) the exact tag or (b) other tags containing the search term, regardless of tag type
{quote}

This test passes currently because it uses the old search, but when you enable the new search by default, the test fails.

Either the search system needs to be fixed to match the behavior outlined in the help, or the help and the automated test need to be modified.

The button title for removing oneself as a co-creator on the Edit Work page or the Edit Series page is titled "Remove Me As Author" and should be "Remove Me As Co-Creator."

Also, the success and error messages you get when using these buttons should refer to creators, not authors:

* Successfully removing yourself from a series should be: {{You have been removed as a creator from the series and its works.}}
* Unsuccessfully removing yourself from a series (because one of the works in said series has only you as a creator) should be: {{Sorry, we can't remove all creators of a work.}}
* Successfully removing yourself from a work should be: {{You have been removed as a creator from the work.}}

The “Remove Me as Co-Creator” option on the mass edit page should have the “As” capitalized now. (You’ll need to select at least one work with a co-creator to make that option appear.)

In the first deploy after Elasticsearch 6.0 has been activated for all users, the following notice should be added to the top of the [Search and Browse FAQ|http://archiveofourown.org/faq/search-and-browse]:


{code:html}
<p class="notice">Our search engine has recently been updated, and this FAQ is based on our old version. We're working on bringing you more up-to-date information, but in the meantime, you can find out more in our <a href="https://archiveofourown.org/admin_posts/10575">news post announcing the search and filter updates</a>!</p>
{code}

*Testing notes*
