column27:
Our [help file|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/ebdee593cbb6ce5fa2362b5db68d148ae7c19118/public/help/skins-creating.html#L32] and [ArchiveConfig.SUPPORTED_CSS_PROPERTIES |https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/f5816199dcb2facc8384ba602c2b9fa53fbd7034/config/config.yml#L296] both say we allow the CSS filter property in skins, which is true, but we fail to allow the necessary values to actually make it useful.

Syntax we should allow, copied from [MDN's filter page|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/filter#Syntax]:

{code:css}filter: blur(5px);
filter: brightness(0.4);
filter: contrast(200%);
filter: drop-shadow(16px 16px 20px blue);
filter: grayscale(50%);
filter: hue-rotate(90deg);
filter: invert(75%);
filter: opacity(25%);
filter: saturate(30%);
filter: sepia(60%);{code}

(We don't allow SVGs to be used in skins at this time, so we can leave off the url("some_file.svg") value that is also mentioned on that page.) 

*What currently happens:*
If you enter something like 

{code:css}.icon img { filter: blur(10em); }{code}

 in a skin, you get an error like:

{quote}Sorry\! We couldn't save this skin because:{quote}

* The filter property in .icon img cannot have the value blur(10em), sorry\!
* There don't seem to be any rules for .icon img

*Notes:* 
Ideally, we should also allow multiple filters, e.g. 

{code:css}.icon img { filter: contrast(175%) brightness(3%) }{code}

Due to the [regex we use to allow rotate for the transform property|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/6473c3a184c66225edb121ced72332d93b2482be/lib/css_cleaner.rb#L15], it's currently possible to use the hue-rotate and grayscale values.

*Testing:*
Try using each the examples copied from MDN in a site skin or a work skin. The skin should save without an error and with the filter you entered.

