column27:
To prevent duplicates, the mass import API checks if the archivist has already bookmarked the external work currently being bookmarked. To do this, it filters the archivist's bookmarks on {{bookmarkable}} with a {{url}} field set to the external work's url. Unfortunately, if the bookmarkable is a work or series, it doesn't have a url field so this code crashes if the archivist has ever bookmarked anything that isn't an external work.

*Testing Notes*
This is covered by an automated test but can be tested manually from a REST client by sending the following POST request (this format can be pasted into RubyMine, or adapted to a REST client - token for Test will be provided on request):

{code}
POST https://test.archiveofourown.org/api/v2/bookmarks/search
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Token token={{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "archivist": "testy", "bookmarks": [{"url":"http://example.com"}] }
{code}

Right now, this test will return the following response:

{code}
{
  "status": "internal_server_error",
  "messages": "An error occurred in the Archive code: undefined method `url' for #<Work:0x007fcb31b322f8>"
}
{code}

But after the fix the expect response should be:

{code}
{
  "status": "ok",
  "messages": [
    "Successfully searched bookmarks for archivist 'testy'"
  ],
  "bookmarks": [
    {
      "status": "not_found",
      "archive_url": "",
      "original_id": "123",
      "original_url": "http://example.com",
      "messages": [
        "There is no bookmark for testy and the URL http://example.com"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{code}

The mass import API returns human-readable messages whenever it performs an action on a user's behalf. Because I'm an idiot, sometimes this is a single string and sometimes an array.

*Testing*
Given that {{url1}} is imported and {{url2}} is not, the following REST request:

{code}
POST https://test.archiveofourown.org/api/v2/works/search
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Token token={{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "works": [{ "original_urls": ["{{url1}}", "{{url2}}"] }] }
{code}

results in a response that looks like this:

{code}
{
  "status": "ok",
  "messages": [
    "Successfully searched all provided URLs."
  ],
  "works": [
    {
      "status": "found",
      "original_id": "",
      "original_url": "http://localhost:3010/opendoorstempsite/chapters/1",
      "search_results": [
        {
          "archive_url": "https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/2",
          "created": "2008-09-13T07:46:07.000-04:00",
          "message": "Work \"Title\", created on 2008-09-13 was found at \"https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/2\"."
        }
      ],
      "messages": "Work \"Title\", created on 2008-09-13 was found at \"https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/2\"."
    },
    {
      "status": "not_found",
      "original_id": "",
      "original_url": "http://localhost:3010/opendoorstempsite/chapters/12",
      "messages": [
        ""
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{code}

Note that the {{messages}} in the response for the first work is a string, and in the second work, it's an array (and an empty one to boot).

The response should be:

{code}
{
  "status": "ok",
  "messages": [
    "Successfully searched all provided URLs."
  ],
  "works": [
    {
      "status": "found",
      "original_id": "",
      "original_url": "http://localhost:3010/opendoorstempsite/chapters/1",
      "search_results": [
        {
          "archive_url": "https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/2",
          "created": "2008-09-13T07:46:07.000-04:00",
          "message": "Work \"Title\", created on 2008-09-13 was found at \"https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/2\"."
        }
      ],
      "messages": [
          "Work \"Title\", created on 2008-09-13 was found at \"https://test.archiveofourown.org/works/2\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "status": "not_found",
      "original_id": "",
      "original_url": "http://localhost:3010/opendoorstempsite/chapters/12",
      "messages": [
        "No work has been imported from http://localhost:3010/opendoorstempsite/chapters/12"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{code}

