column154:
19/Aug/19 8:40 PM;557058:fa089759-8cd1-4db3-b506-5731a37fd5a6;{quote}*The series was listed under Current Series, and my co-creator received an email saying they had been added to the series – this is* *_before_* *I cleared up the errors. In fact, I once again chose to cancel what I was doing at this stage… but it turns out the work had been added to the series, so at least the co-creator email makes sense. (I don’t really think the work should have been added to the series, though.)*{quote}

This is a pre-existing bug. Series are saved and added to the work as soon as you assign the attributes, even if you’re previewing, and even if the other changes to the work are invalid. Basically, they have the exact same issue that collections do: [https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-5556|https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-5556|smart-link]

I think the series version of this bug is easier to clear up than the collections version, though, so let me know if you want me to add it to the release.



{quote}*Yes, I can add/remove both owners and moderators, but I still need to specify the username if the pseud is not unique (AO3-4867). If I am logged in as nivens and add sarken (sarken) as both an owner and moderator, and then try to* *_remove_* *sarken (sarken) from both fields at once, it only removes sarken as an owner – I have to try a second time to make it remove them as a moderator. Not sure if that’s normal behavior.*{quote}

I’m pretty sure that’s the pre-existing behavior (though it might be worth a bug report). The {{owner_changes}} parameter is processed before the {{moderator_changes}} parameter (because it’s first in the call to permit). The call to {{owner_changes=}} causes the user to be completely removed as both owner and moderator. So when {{moderator_changes=}} is called, it treats it as adding a new moderator, since the user no longer has any relationship with the OwnedTagSet.

(The reason I wanted to test tagset ownerships is because at one point the PR included some more serious changes to {{parse_bylines}}, which is used in both {{owner_changes=}} and {{moderator_changes=}}. The changes have been reverted for the most part, so it pretty much just needs a quick check to make sure nothing unexpected occurs when parsing bylines.)



{quote}*Used it to remove myself from a work in a series. It worked, but I stayed on the series despite not having any other works in the series.*{quote}

This is how it works when removing yourself from a work on Beta, I believe. Maybe this should be another bug in the same vein as [https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-5332|https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-5332|smart-link]

