column147:
09/Feb/20 6:17 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;[~accountid:557058:fa089759-8cd1-4db3-b506-5731a37fd5a6]:
{quote}
AO3-5859 is supposed to replace pseud_id with user_id for all kudos queries, but the commentable_id, commentable_type, user_id index is only going to be added in the big migration. Have you double-checked to make sure the performance is going to be okay for the week or two after AO3-5859 is live but before that index gets added?
{quote}

We'll be running some benchmarks (from ticking):
{code}
work = Work.find(234222)Benchmark.bmbm do |x|
  %i(pseud_id user_id).each do |field|
    {
      guest: work.kudos.where(field => nil),
      non_guest: work.kudos.where.not(field => nil)
    }.each_pair do |name, relation|
      x.report("#{field} #{name} count") { relation.all.count }
      x.report("#{field} #{name} any") { relation.all.any? }
      x.report("#{field} #{name} load") { relation.order(created_at: :desc).all.load }
    end
  end   
end
{code}

If kudos queries (on works) take a noticeable performance hit, then we should be doing AO3-5868 separately, and before this issue.

column149:
11/Feb/20 8:18 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;Not very promising numbers. [~accountid:557058:fa089759-8cd1-4db3-b506-5731a37fd5a6]:
{quote}
I think a cache hit currently does only one kudos query: pseud_id non_guest any. According to the benchmarks, that's currently around 1ms for that work, and would go up to 69ms for the user_id version of that query. That would happen every time that work is viewed.
{quote}

We'll be cautious and do AO3-5868 + AO3-5869 first.

