column150:
31/Jul/20 4:21 PM;557058:fa089759-8cd1-4db3-b506-5731a37fd5a6;{quote}in anonymous mode the form for submitting the comments is still visible and open.{quote}

Did it stay that way? Work caching is enabled, so most changes aren’t going to be reflected for logged-out users until the cache has expired (~40 minutes, IIRC, though it might have increased since), and I’m not sure there’s anything I can do to fix that. But if it didn’t eventually resolve itself, that might indicate that something else is wrong.

{quote}it does not bounce with an error when the comment option is disabled mid-typing for anonymous users{quote}

After poking around, it looks like the {{after_action :check_for_flash}} hook, which is intended to make sure that flash messages are displayed to logged-out users even if the page is cached, doesn’t work if you redirect in a {{before_action}} hook (since that [stops the callback chain|https://api.rubyonrails.org/classes/AbstractController/Callbacks/ClassMethods.html#method-i-before_action], if I’m understanding it properly). I’ll have to think about a clean way to fix that. (Maybe overriding {{redirect_to}} so that it automatically calls {{check_for_flash}}?)

