column154:
23/Jul/21 3:14 PM;557058:fa089759-8cd1-4db3-b506-5731a37fd5a6;{quote}But\! One thing that seemed kind of weird is that, on the edit page, the Categories tags were checked and the Additional Tags weren’t. (The instructions say “Check to remove.”) I don’t know if that’s normal.{quote}

It is normal, apparently. The [checkboxes in the ratings/warnings/categories sections|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/c981777f3983b5d114f12dc6757542cbe4535cb3/app/views/owned_tag_sets/_internal_tag_set_fields.html.erb#L26] are for {{"#{tag_type}_tagnames"}}, instead of {{"#{tag_type}_tags_to_remove"}} like they are [for the fandom/characters/relationships/freeforms sections|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/c981777f3983b5d114f12dc6757542cbe4535cb3/app/views/owned_tag_sets/_internal_tag_set_fields.html.erb#L11]. Might be good to change the text to clarify, though I’m not sure that’s in scope.

{quote}I could not actually save changes to 15778 because I got the error “Request: Your Request cannot include any additional tag tags, but you have included (1)”. This is something of a problem because the moderator cannot allow additional tags when there are already sign-ups, *but* I don’t know that it’s a huge one: we don’t know if it will affect any challenges or if we’re dealing with a hypothetical.{quote}

I don’t think this can be fixed without an overhaul of the way that challenges handle tags.

(Changing the tag type also interacts with the minimum/maximum tag count of each type, and any match settings for gift exchanges. To make sure that no sign-ups become invalid, and everything is working as the moderator intended when they first set up the challenge, you’d need all of the categories that were changed to freeforms to still count as categories, but only for some exchanges. So you’d need to introduce (a) prompt fields that permit tags of multiple types, and (b) prompt fields that only permit a subset of the freeforms listed in the tag set. Which might be useful for other reasons, but would probably hold up the release by several months.)

column27:
We no longer support Open ID as of 2012 (AO3-3275). Ergo we should remove the tables open_id_authentication_associations and open_id_authentication_nonces.

To test, a database admin should run the migration, up and down and up again.

{{bundle exec rake db:migrate:up VERSION=20230106203903}}

{{bundle exec rake db:migrate:down VERSION=20230106203903}}

